When dozens of agents work in one repo, they collide. These tools use git refs as cheap, atomic locks so they don't:

- **gh-issue-lease**: an agent leases a GitHub issue before working on it, so two agents never take the same task.
- **gh-once**: makes an action run exactly once across all agents.
- **gh-worktree-gc**: cleans up stale agent worktrees.

They came out of building HailTrigger with parallel agents, and are published on npm.
